Rule 1 (inputs must be broadcastable across all dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, (if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) else ndim(v_2)) - 1] : (ndim(v_1) - i - 1 < 0 ∨ ndim(v_2) - i - 1 < 0 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1))
>>
Rule 2 (leading aligned dimension must be compatible for broadcasting)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 1) then (shape(v_1, if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) - ndim(v_2) else 0) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, if ndim(v_2) ≥ ndim(v_1) then ndim(v_2) - ndim(v_1) else 0) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) - ndim(v_2) else 0) = shape(v_2, if ndim(v_2) ≥ ndim(v_1) then ndim(v_2) - ndim(v_1) else 0))
>>
Rule 4 (out tensor must have boolean dtype)
{v_3 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_3) = 0
>>
Rule 6 (input and other must have tensor dtypes in the supported range 0–10)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= 0 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10 ∧ 0 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 10
